! mcp_bootstrap_p255.strap -- MCP printed page 255: the Input Program's
! error-recovery section, continued (LVI,$15,RKC+1.0 .. SIC,(VP)),
! lines 1-56.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.6, read at 400 dpi (900 dpi for the
! name/statement glyphs).  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP  CARD ID 0B000432  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 255"
! (round glyphs in numeric fields read 0); the heading row's LOCATION
! field is 230317, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, all located, contiguous from 230317.00 to
! 230353.40 (a half word; next location 230354.00), then blank paper.
! printed p.254 (PDF p.5) ends with line 52 "RESTOR LV,VU,0.32($13)" at
! 230316.40, so line 1 continues it; printed p.256 (PDF p.7, heading
! LOCATION 230354) opens at 230354.00.  No remarks.  Asterisks after the
! LOCATION on lines 15 and 37.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 11 statement "REDUMP": the D prints with a worn stem; spelled
!     as landed p.243 (REDUMP SYN, (8)230400.0) and C22-6728 (12 times).
!   * line 35 label RECDMP: third glyph round/open (C), fourth has a
!     straight left stem (D) at 900 dpi.  No other deck spells it;
!     C22-6728 OCR prints "RECCMP" once, a flowchart box (does not
!     close it).  Nothing references it here: rests on ink alone.
!   * line 45 label REDMP: third glyph has a stem (D); landed p.219
!     B,REDMP prints 230346.10 = this row.
!   * lines 18/19 "RECCW": both round glyphs open, no stem; written
!     RECCW (RE + CCW, as RDCCW on p.249).  VF prints 230371.00+.
!   * line 27 REJJOB: as landed decks; BZBZ prints 230364.77.
!   * line 42 ",DCCMM" = ,DCOMM (worn O): landed p.105 DCOMM 35.32;
!     prints 000043.40.
!   * line 47 "VFCNT" (sheet read VECNT): F is plain ink; landed VFCNT.
!   * line 52 a stray dot between LOCATION and BINARY: speck, ignored.
!   * line 44 ",4.C" = ,4.0 (open round in a numeric field); prints
!     000004.00.
!   * hex/octal round glyphs read 0 throughout ("C0" etc.).
!
! EXTERNALS FROM THIS PAGE'S BINARY ONLY: RECCW (230371.0, VF line 18
! BIT-EXACT), RWMSGE (230374.0, lines 40/43 BIT-EXACT as half-word
! address constants).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials run 0B000432 .. 0B000458.  Shared:
! 1-2 (432), 3-4 (433), 6-9 (435), 13-14 (439), 15-18 (440), 19-20
! (441), 22-24 (443), 28-29 (447), 30-32 (448), 33-34 (449), 35-36
! (450), 37-40 (451), 41-44 (452), 45-46 (453), 47-48 (454), 49-50
! (455), 52-55 (457).  Line 56's 458 is also p.256 line 1's
! (CB+,VP,VRJTP -- SIC and its branch on one card).  No serial skipped.
!
! THE PAGE ENDS IN A BARE SIC.  Line 56 SIC,(VP)'s branch half is
! printed p.256 line 1 (CB+,VP,VRJTP at 230354.00).  strap_asm refuses
! a SIC with nothing after it ("SIC must be immediately followed ...
! found 'end of program'"), so a scaffold "SLC, (8)230354.0" (p.256's
! own origin, compiles nothing, skips nothing) follows line 56 for the
! standalone verify.  In a merged build p.256's identical origin SLC
! follows it; scaffolding the CB+ itself instead would deposit 230354.00
! twice and the merge refuses that (tested).

